    <desc>What <app>Pano Terminal</app> is and what it offers.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Introduction</title>

<p><app>Pano Terminal</app> is a terminal emulator application for accessing a
  UNIX shell environment which can be used to run programs available on your
  system. It is a fork of <app>GNOME Terminal</app> and can be installed next
  to it: the two keep their own profiles and preferences.</p>

  <p><app>Pano Terminal</app> supports escape sequences that control cursor
  position and colors. Besides what <app>GNOME Terminal</app> offers, it
  has:</p>

  <list>
    <item><p><link xref="gs-split-panes">Split panes</link>, and
    <link xref="gs-tabs">tabs</link> at the top, bottom, left or right of the
    window.</p></item>
    <item><p><link xref="gs-session">Session restore</link> of windows, tabs
    and panes.</p></item>
    <item><p><link xref="cmd-shell-integration">Shell integration</link> for
    bash, zsh and fish: marks for each command, jumping between prompts,
    copying the output of a command, and
    <link xref="cmd-notifications">notifications</link> when long commands
    finish.</p></item>
    <item><p>A <link xref="cmd-palette">command palette</link> and
    <link xref="txt-quick-select">quick select</link>.</p></item>
    <item><p>A <link xref="gs-quick-terminal">quick terminal</link> that you
    show and hide with one key.</p></item>
    <item><p>About 240 <link xref="app-colors">color schemes</link>,
    transparent backgrounds, and a <link xref="app-window">header bar</link>
    in the colors of the terminal.</p></item>
  </list>

